# Line endings, and why they are pinned here.
#
# The files under assets/vendor/ and the deployed build (assets/js/app.<hash>.js,
# assets/css/app.<hash>.css, assets/build-manifest.json) are loaded with
# Subresource Integrity: the browser hashes the bytes it receives and blocks the
# file when they differ from the hash recorded in VENDOR.json or
# build-manifest.json. A checkout that rewrites LF to CRLF changes exactly those
# bytes, and the page then fails with "failed to find a valid digest in the
# integrity attribute" — which is what happened on a Windows clone of this
# repository (QA-3 deploy hotfix).
#
# So: LF in the repository, LF in the working tree, on every platform. There is
# no autocrlf setting anywhere that can win over an attribute.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Hashed byte-for-byte — never converted, never normalized.
assets/vendor/** -text
assets/js/app.js -text
assets/js/app.*.js -text
assets/css/app.css -text
assets/css/app.*.css -text
assets/build-manifest.json -text
